{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And one who strikes his father or his mother shall surely be put to death.</b> The Sages have already taught that his execution is by strangulation (Sanhedrin 84a). Therefore Scripture placed next to it <b>And one who steals a person and sells him</b>, for that too is in the same manner of execution, and separated from it <b>And one who curses his father or his mother</b>, because that is by stoning, for it is stated concerning it: \"his father and his mother he cursed; his blood is upon him\" (Leviticus 20:9), and everyone concerning whom this language is stated is by stoning (Sanhedrin 66a), as derived from what is written: \"with stones they shall be stoned; their blood is upon them\" (Leviticus 20:27). And He made the punishment of the one who curses more severe than the punishment of the one who strikes, because the sin of cursing is more prevalent, since the fool, when he grows angry and becomes enraged, curses the king and his father and his mother continually all the day, and the transgression according to its prevalence always requires great correction. Or because there is in cursing a greater sin, for it involves invoking the name of YHWH (Shevuot 36a), and so he must be punished for his sin against his father and his mother, and for having borne the name of YHWH his Elohim for transgression and sin. And the Gaon Rav Saadia said that he placed the matter of one who steals a person between them, because in most cases those stolen are children, and they grow up in another place and do not recognize their fathers, and it may come about that they strike them and curse them; therefore it is fitting to punish the kidnapper with death like them, for the punishment falls upon him."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:13:14.735153170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}